# Design skills (GameCon)

Three toolkits are installed for UI / marketing / brand work:

1. **design-taste-frontend** (taste skill) — `.claude/skills/design-taste-frontend/`
   Anti-slop frontend: one system, one section per screen, real product visuals,
   motion + browser finish gate. Read `SKILL.md` before building or polishing
   landings, marketing pages, or public guest surfaces.

2. **open-design** — `.claude/skills/open-design/`
   Catalogue binder. Content clone: `~/.open-design-skill/repo` (or `$OPEN_DESIGN_ROOT`).
   Project binding: `.open-design.json`. List helpers:
   `node .claude/skills/open-design/scripts/list-design-systems.mjs` (and
   `list-design-templates.mjs`, `list-skills.mjs`, `list-craft.mjs`).

3. **awesome-design-md** — `design-refs/awesome-design-md/<brand>/DESIGN.md`
   84 brand specs (apple, nike, spotify, spacex, playstation, …). When the user
   says «сделай в этом стиле» / «make it in this style», open that brand’s
   `DESIGN.md` and apply its vocabulary to GameCon UI **without** copying logos
   or trademarked wordmarks.

## Source of truth

- Project system: root `DESIGN.md` (GameCon tokens + composition rules).
- CSS tokens: `resources/css/app.css` `@theme` / `--color-gc-*`.
- Do not invent a parallel palette.

## When to invoke

| User asks… | Do… |
|---|---|
| Restyle / landing / «looks AI» | Read taste skill → apply house rules → browser-check if shipping |
| Deck / prototype / brand audit / «open design» | Follow open-design skill phases; honor `.open-design.json` |
| «В стиле Apple / Nike / …» | Load `design-refs/awesome-design-md/<slug>/DESIGN.md` |

## Install / refresh (if missing)

```bash
npx skills add https://github.com/Leonxlnx/taste-skill --skill design-taste-frontend -a cursor -a claude-code -y
npx skills add sugarforever/open-design-skill -a cursor -a claude-code -y
test -d "${OPEN_DESIGN_ROOT:-$HOME/.open-design-skill/repo}" \
  || git clone --depth 1 https://github.com/nexu-io/open-design.git "${OPEN_DESIGN_ROOT:-$HOME/.open-design-skill/repo}"
```

Brand pack is already vendored under `design-refs/awesome-design-md/` (from
[VoltAgent/awesome-design-md](https://github.com/VoltAgent/awesome-design-md)).
